          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Withdrawal of the Invasion Troops</strong><br>\nUnder international pressure, British, French, and Israeli troops eventually withdrew from Egypt. The Suez Canal remained under Egyptian control, and the Suez Crisis marked the end of traditional colonial power in the region.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Long-term Effects</strong><br>\nThe Suez Crisis had long-term effects on international politics. It demonstrated the limited power of traditional European colonial powers and strengthened the position of the United States and the Soviet Union as global superpowers.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Lessons from the Suez Crisis</strong><br>\nThe Suez Crisis taught the world about changes in the geopolitical landscape and the importance of self-determination and national sovereignty. It also highlighted the growing significance of international institutions like the United Nations in resolving global conflicts.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
